  "notes": "Synthetic subset of the same #1739 R2FAIR run shown in the cross-dataset comparison. Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct; Spearman rho_frozen across evaluation contexts at training-frozen layers, not within-condition Pearson. Six values: 3 traits x 2 methods. Both methods share 200 graded-trait targets per trait (5 instruction pairs x 2 signs x 20 held-out questions). Synthetic suite derived from the Persona Vectors extraction/evaluation pipeline, not the paper monitoring experiment of 8 interpolated system prompts. Map trained on generic WildChat plus eliciting training pairs (ADD); label-free PV projection arms. Point estimates and 95% CIs are copied exactly from the underlying all_arms_spearman.json transfer rows. Intervals resample evaluation contexts at fixed models/layers, not shared prompt or question clusters; no training-seed uncertainty. Code-inherited on-policy recipe: 5 responses per context, temperature 1, 1024-token cap, top_p not explicitly pinned; banked Sonnet4.5 graded judgments with rejudge recovery. Realized collection settings have not been independently rechecked against every completion manifest. No generation or judging rerun. This replaces the unrelated historical #779 within-condition Pearson slice mistakenly selected for the opening.",
